     groupSort.getSort(), sortWithinGroup.getSort(), totalHitCount, totalGroupedHitCount, groupDocsArr, Float.NaN
);
```
Reason:
The `groupSort` variable was incorrectly used to determine the sorting criteria for grouped results, which caused the sorting behavior to be incorrect when the `group.sort` option was specified in queries. The `transformToNativeShardDoc` method was called with `groupSort`, leading to improper sorting of documents within groups.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
ScoreDoc[] scoreDocs = transformToNativeShardDoc(documents, sortWithinGroup, shard, schema);
```
```java
TopGroups<BytesRef> topGroups = new TopGroups<>(
